highlights:
Model Scaling Laws: (1) Reynolds Model Law (predominant viscous forces: $Re_m = Re_p \implies  rac{ho_m V_m L_m}{\mu_m} =  rac{ho_p V_p L_p}{\mu_p}$; Velocity ratio $V_r =  rac{
u_r}{L_r}$, Time ratio $T_r =  rac{L_r^2}{
u_r}$, Discharge ratio $Q_r = 
u_r L_r$, Force ratio $F_r = ho_r V_r^2 L_r^2$); (2) Froude Model Law (predominant gravity forces: $Fr_m = Fr_p \implies  rac{V_m}{\sqrt{g_m L_m}} =  rac{V_p}{\sqrt{g_p L_p}}$; Velocity ratio $V_r = \sqrt{L_r}$, Time ratio $T_r = \sqrt{L_r}$, Discharge ratio $Q_r = L_r^{5/2}$, Force ratio $F_r = ho_r L_r^3$).
